# Feature 9 — Authentication & Onboarding

## Goal
Allow users to sign in and create accounts using email/password, 
and select their role during onboarding. Google Sign-In will be 
added later once OKTA approval is confirmed.

## Sign-In Flow
1. User lands on the login page
2. Email and password fields
3. "Sign in" button (yellow #FFEA00, #222629 text)
4. Toggle to "Create account" mode for new users
5. After successful sign-in:
   - If first time user → redirect to /onboarding
   - If returning user → redirect to /dashboard

## Create Account Flow
1. Email input
2. Password input
3. Confirm password input
4. "Create account" button (yellow #FFEA00)
5. On success: create Firestore profile, redirect to /onboarding

## Onboarding Flow (First-Time Users)
- Welcome screen with role selection
- "Welcome to Lahjah!"
- Subtext: "Tell us what you do so we can set up your workspace."
- Role selection (large card buttons, single select):

  DESIGNER card:
  - Title: "Designer"
  - Description: "Create copy requests, generate copy, and submit 
    for review."

  COPY TEAM card:
  - Title: "Copy Team"
  - Description: "Review copy requests, leave feedback, and approve 
    submissions."

- "Get started" button — yellow #FFEA00, disabled until role selected
- On continue: save role to Firestore, redirect to /dashboard

## Data Structure
On first sign-up, create Firestore document under users/{uid}:
- uid (Firebase Auth UID)
- email
- role ("designer" | "copy_team")
- createdAt (timestamp)
- onboardingCompleted (boolean — true after role selected)

## Auth Guard Behavior
- All protected pages check for valid auth
- If signed in but onboardingCompleted is false → redirect to /onboarding
- If signed in and onboardingCompleted is true → allow access by role

## Firestore Security Rules
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null 
        && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }
    match /requests/{requestId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
    }
  }
}

